    "winner": "unknown",
    "clashSummary": "ZEN vs DAN DANNAH took place at **Ministry of Sound** during the **PenGame Cold War Finals** event, with PenGame Rap Battles powered by SoundOn. The host introduces it as a heavyweight clash and brings both battlers to the stage.\n\nZEN goes first.\n\nZEN opens with his usual identity markers: **“C to the E N,” “long-haired Leng man,” “Grandmaster Mic Man,”** and **PenGame champ**. His first round is built around DAN DANNAH’s age, appearance and battle persona. He attacks DAN’s greying image, flips Daniel-son and Karate Kid references, brings in Cobra Kai, Hancock, Alien vs Predator, dandelion wordplay, Wall-E imagery and Spider-Man web/body references. He closes by repeating that he is built for war and that North men are getting killed in the war.\n\nDAN DANNAH responds with a stronger and more direct first round. He opens by saying everybody calls him Dan because he is “the Dan” and “the man.” He moves into punch, chokeslam, monkey/orangutan, Afghanistan/Taliban, Bruce Wayne, batarang, Jackie Chan and armbar references. He frames ZEN’s “redemption arc” as something that will fail, says he will rip ZEN in half, and ends by calling himself **ZEN’s killer**. DAN’s round is more controlled and lands as the cleaner opener.\n\nZEN’s second round switches style. He focuses on DAN DANNAH’s family, using a DJ father and guitarist mother angle. The round is packed with music and sexual wordplay: spinning like tracks, guitar/wood, Facebook, recording booths, holding D, musical chords, G-strings and sound systems. He then moves into sister material, Ginger Jay, graveyard/reverse imagery and a PenGame champ claim. It is creative and personal, but also heavy with family-based battle material.\n\nDAN DANNAH’s second round is more structured. He attacks ZEN for having an old flow, saying he has been rapping the same way since 2008 and needs to show growth. He brings in Pinocchio nose imagery, says ZEN lost to JM and should stop saying he got robbed, flips courts/witness/snitching, then moves into ballistics, Father Christmas, Nagini, veteran/passive clash, running out of breath, JM flashbacks and ZEN’s lack of relevance. DAN’s second is sharper and more opponent-specific.\n\nZEN’s third round is the strongest visible ZEN round in the transcript. He attacks DAN’s age by comparing him to Pete & Bas, then builds into a gaming/controller scheme. He uses a **GTA San Andreas cheat-code** sequence, with the host even stopping the round to check whether the code is legitimate. ZEN then moves into Spider-Man, gym/body, Nigerian dad, Trappy pad/turtle, DJ/Mac-10/deck, Sidemen, KSI, university, 2-1 degree, Sun Tzu, teeth gap, Michael Myers, Didier Drogba and ex-girlfriend material. It is his clearest room-control moment.\n\nThe transcript cuts off after ZEN’s third round, meaning DAN DANNAH’s third is missing.\n\nThere is no official judgement or host result included. Because of that, the final winner should not be recorded as official from this transcript alone.",
