        "performer": "K.I.M.E",
        "overview": "K.I.M.E wins because the judges favour his delivery, aggression and overall story. He brings consistent pressure across all three rounds and finishes strongly enough to take the decision.\n\nHis first round is aggressive and direct. He uses school/classroom imagery, physical threats, smoke, candy crush, bluff and college material. The round is dense and full of attacks, showing K.I.M.E is not there to play.\n\nHis second round is his most technical. The “backstreet/backseat,” “Balamin,” “battery,” “Barking/Battersea,” and “galaxy” sections show he can layer wordplay. Some of the material is messy or very fast, but the aggression is constant.\n\nHis third round wins him the battle in the judges’ eyes. He performs with more authority, brings PenGame North energy, and closes with stronger presence. The “taste of defeat,” “gospel boy,” “nostrils bigger than Efton’s,” and fatherhood/name angle give him enough clear moments to edge the battle.\n\nK.I.M.E’s biggest strength is attack density. He keeps punching, even when the writing gets rough.",
