        "performer": "iiiBEREALZ",
        "overview": "iiiBEREALZ wins because he has the stronger first and third rounds. His second is also competitive, but his final round is the cleanest and most decisive closer in the battle.\n\nHis first round is very direct. He does not just respond to TRAPPY’s insults; he attacks TRAPPY’s whole image. The stolen-bars angle, recycled-material angle and dead-videos angle give the round more bite. He makes TRAPPY look like someone with style but not originality.\n\nHis second round is more aggressive and personal. He attacks TRAPPY’s music, teeth, eyes, ego and fainting at the finals. He also brings battle-culture references, accusing TRAPPY of stealing from bigger names. This round is close, but TRAPPY’s second has the better structure.\n\nHis third is the battle-winning round. iiiBEREALZ moves like a veteran in the final. The Hannibal Lecter body-disposal section is clean, the “catching bodies” repetition works, and the references to God’s Plan, Mob Ties, Batman/Bane, Cain and Abel, and Nas give the round replay value. He ends with enough confidence and structure to swing the battle.\n\niiiBEREALZ’s biggest strength is composure. He takes TRAPPY’s attacks and turns the battle into a question of originality, status and pen.",
