        "overview": "TAPPED24 wins this battle because he completes his round, controls the room and gives the only full performance of the clash.\n\nHis biggest strength is confidence. He does not come in carefully; he comes in with a full identity. The “way too dark” section works because it explains his style and gives the crowd a reason to expect harsh material. He then backs it up with family insults, film references, drug allegations, sexuality angles and name flips.\n\nThe Will Smith section is one of the most structured parts of the battle. He connects **Bad Boys**, **Men in Black**, **Suicide Squad**, **8 Mile**, **Hancock**, and **Ragnarok** into a long pop-culture run. It gives the round more shape than just random insults.\n\nThe “J Money” hook at the end is also effective. It turns JMUNI’s name into a chant and gives TAPPED24 a clean closer. In a one-round battle, ending with something memorable matters.\n\nTAPPED24’s material is often offensive and shock-based, but as a battle performance, he is much more complete than JMUNI here.",
