        "overview": "SEVZ wins this one-rounder because his material is more layered, more current, and more consistently aimed at DRIZZGB. His round has clearer sections and stronger replay value.\n\nHe begins with a status gap, saying DRIZZGB is not close to his level. From there, he moves into several clean themes: Rishi Sunak, graveyard/dead-you, cousin chemistry, Orion ID, cross-eyed/tic-tac-toe, identity, Jammer/Lord of the Mics, Boy Better Know, JME, Trappy’s shadow, Aladdin, Will Smith and adoption angles.\n\nThe strongest part of SEVZ’s round is the way he strings references together. The “Lord of the Mics / Jammer / Boy Better Know / JME” section works because it directly attacks DRIZZGB’s grime identity. The “Trappy carried you for nine rounds” line is also a strong scene-specific closer because it attacks DRIZZGB’s battle reputation rather than just his appearance.\n\nSEVZ’s biggest strength is structure. In a one-round battle, he gives a full arc: status gap, identity attack, scene credibility, pop-culture punches, and a final reputation kill.",
