        "overview": "DRIZZGB has a strong showing and does not get washed, but he loses because SEVZ’s round is cleaner and more layered.\n\nHis best section is the early youth/dependence angle. The Rizla, Red Bull, mum pulling socks up, mum wiping snot and uni/grades material gives him a clear way to make SEVZ look childish. That angle is easy to understand and works well in a one-round setting.\n\nHe also has good aggression in the middle and back end of the round. The “severed up / peppered up” wordplay is one of his better name flips, and the “putting this kid in his place” section gives the round weight.\n\nThe issue is that the round has too many restarts and some of the wording becomes messy. He gets through it, but the structure feels less controlled than SEVZ’s. DRIZZGB has good moments, but SEVZ has the stronger full round.",
