        "overview": "K.I.M.E has a very strong round and makes this a close battle. His opening is more layered than F-DON’s and his Marvel scheme is one of the best technical sections in the clash.\n\nHe starts fast with appearance jokes around F-DON’s nostrils, breath and looks. He then transitions into the Marvel run, which is clearly prepared and well thought out. The Thor/Fantastic Four/Iron Man/Spider-Man/Captain/Black Widow/Infinity/Endgame/Eternals/Avengers/Venom/Doomsday sequence shows strong writing and performance ambition.\n\nHe also has strong opponent-specific content. He references F-DON’s PenGame and Don’t Flop past, suggests Dan carried him, attacks the 2v2 final, calls out the five-grand loss, and uses the “F is for…” section to break down F-DON’s name.\n\nThe issue is that the round becomes overcrowded. K.I.M.E throws a lot at F-DON, but F-DON’s response is more direct and easier to score. K.I.M.E has more detail; F-DON has the cleaner finish.\n\nK.I.M.E’s biggest strength is attack density. His biggest weakness is that the round feels overloaded in places.",
