        "overview": "F-DON has a strong first round and moments in the third, but loses because his second round collapses and his third does not match ZEN’s closer.\n\nHis first round is good. The Zendaya rhyme pattern is sharp, the Tory Lanez and Ned Stark lines land, and the “she love a bad man” section gives him a proper crowd moment. He also makes a good angle out of ZEN being in PenGame’s house and needing to show gratitude.\n\nHis second round starts with potential. The Leeds angle, “Kappistan / Kappanese,” capping, martial arts and Capricorn material could have developed into a strong round, but he loses control. The room reacts heavily and the host moves the battle on. That round is hard to score for F-DON.\n\nHis third round is better than the second, but still not enough. He returns to capping, Leeds, acapella, martial arts, Capri Styles, idiot name flips and criticising ZEN’s fast delivery. The problem is that ZEN’s third is much more complete and more layered.\n\nF-DON’s biggest strength is stage presence when locked in. His weakness in this battle is consistency.",
